# Local license election for generated output. ./zero creates .env from this
# template and fills it in; .env is gitignored. Exactly one of the two settings
# below may be active. CI supplies the same variables from secrets.

# Commercial (Speakeasy customers): run `speakeasy auth login`, then `./zero`.
# It fetches a signed license token for your workspace and writes it here.
#SPEAKEASY_LICENSE_TOKEN=

# Open source: accept AGPL-3.0-only licensing for generated output
# (`./zero --license agpl-3.0-only` writes this line).
#SPEAKEASY_GENERATED_LICENSE=agpl-3.0-only

# A self-hosted or staging platform is selected with `./zero --server URL` or an
# exported SPEAKEASY_SERVER_URL; it is deliberately not read from this file.
